# NOTE: keep in step with .containerignore (make check asserts it); only this
# 2-line header differs between the two files.
# Image build context. Everything the Containerfile does not COPY out of the
# host tree is noise at best (-f points at the file, not the context) and a
# cache-invalidating context change at worst, so the whole of the host tooling
# is excluded. container/ and mise.toml are the only things the build reads.
.git
.agents
.github
build
examples
LICENSE
Makefile
README.md
AGENTS.md
CHANGELOG.md
*.log
